1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:02,070
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:03,210
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:05,140
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,010
Chief Cha, wait.

5
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:12,720
Yes?

6
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:17,090
Can we talk for a moment?

7
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:18,690
(Design Team)

8
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,760
Right now?

9
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,560
Yes.

10
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:34,610
Are you kidding me?

11
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:38,480
Hey, Hae Ra.

12
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,050
Hae Ra, and not Ms. Kang?
What's gotten into you?

13
00:00:42,650 --> 00:00:44,580
That's not the issue right now.

14
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:47,250
Seok Jin and Ko Eun Seol
went somewhere together.

15
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:49,050
What?

16
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:03,540
Ko Eun Seol.

17
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:06,570
What's going on here?

18
00:01:11,910 --> 00:01:12,910
Hae Ra.

19
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:18,980
What do you two think you're doing?

20
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:24,790
Aren't you going to tell me?

21
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:29,190
We were just in the middle
of a conversation.

22
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:30,360
About what?

23
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:31,560
It was nothing.

24
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,300
If it's nothing,
then why can't you tell me?

25
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:35,400
Tell me. Now.

26
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:37,970
What were you two talking about?

27
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:40,240
I said tell me now!

28
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:41,470
Team Leader Kang.

29
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:44,340
I asked to speak with him
because I had something to tell him.

30
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:45,910
You did?

31
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:47,980
What could you possibly have to say
to Seok Jin?

32
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:51,050
Hey.

33
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,550
What on earth did you have
to say to him?

34
00:01:54,790 --> 00:01:56,220
Just like you,

35
00:01:56,290 --> 00:01:58,920
he was under the impression
that I leaked fake news.

36
00:01:59,290 --> 00:02:00,730
I was just telling him it wasn't me.

37
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:05,330
Is that true?

38
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,730
I asked if that was true.

39
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:10,970
Team Leader Kang, stop it.

40
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:12,270
Stop what?

41
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,340
I'll go on ahead.

42
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:16,710
I'm sorry for the misunderstanding.

43
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:22,810
Seok Jin!

44
00:02:29,790 --> 00:02:31,060
Hey. Stop right there.

45
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:43,200
Meet with Seok Jin alone
one more time,

46
00:02:43,670 --> 00:02:45,370
and I swear, I won't let it slide.

47
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:48,340
What are you so scared of?

48
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:50,780
What?

49
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,640
The way you're behaving...

50
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:55,880
makes it feel like
I might have a shot.

51
00:02:56,850 --> 00:02:58,150
Hey, Ko Eun Seol.

52
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:03,760
So,

53
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:06,620
don't provoke me for no reason.

54
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:15,400
That little... Hey!

55
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:18,570
(Planning Director's Office)

56
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:23,010
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

57
00:03:27,350 --> 00:03:28,350
What's this?

58
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:30,820
Ms. Kang dropped it in my office.

59
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:32,380
Oh, dear.

60
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:34,850
Seok Jin, that necklace...

61
00:03:35,050 --> 00:03:36,050
It's actually mine.

62
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:48,530
Ms. Joo, it's almost time
for your appointment.

63
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:49,530
Aren't you leaving?

64
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,240
I should.

65
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:55,870
You should leave now
if you want to be on time.

66
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:10,460
Unbelievable.
She's actually keeping me waiting.

67
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,400
Professor Hong Seok Gyu?

68
00:04:22,170 --> 00:04:23,330
Director Joo Mi Ran?

69
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:26,500
Yes. I'm a bit late, aren't I?

70
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:29,070
I'm sorry.
Have you been waiting long?

71
00:04:29,610 --> 00:04:32,040
No, I just got here myself.

72
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,250
Please, have a seat.

73
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:41,790
You've heard, haven't you?

74
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,820
The Cheongma Scholarship Foundation
is seeking a new board member.

75
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:46,690
Yes.

76
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:48,960
So, are you interested?

77
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,360
I am,

78
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,030
but I'd like to hear
more details first.

79
00:04:54,570 --> 00:04:55,700
More details?

80
00:04:56,830 --> 00:04:58,570
What specifically
are you curious about?

81
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:02,340
For instance, what the work entails.

82
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:04,140
The work
of a foundation board member...

83
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:05,240
is pretty much all the same.

84
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,910
You come in when there's an agenda
and participate in the vote.

85
00:05:08,110 --> 00:05:09,110
Things like that.

86
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:10,880
I'm also curious about the terms.

87
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:13,180
Every time you come in,
under the name of professional fees,

88
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,690
we provide a few thousand dollars.

89
00:05:14,990 --> 00:05:16,590
And I believe
the annual advisory fee...

90
00:05:16,590 --> 00:05:18,920
is around 30,000 dollars.

91
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,390
It's not about the money.

92
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:24,700
Professor, if your name is added...

93
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:27,630
to the scholarship foundation's
board of directors,

94
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:31,500
you'll be flooded with consulting
and lecture requests.

95
00:05:33,270 --> 00:05:37,040
So, all I have to do is accept?

96
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:40,680
No, that's not it.

97
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:43,150
I asked to see you
because you're a candidate.

98
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:46,320
Wait, a candidate?

99
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:47,650
Yes.

100
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:50,390
To be honest,
someone close to CEO Kang...

101
00:05:50,390 --> 00:05:51,760
will likely get the position.

102
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:55,760
But I wanted to give
the Chairman some backing,

103
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:57,400
which is why I asked
to see you, Professor.

104
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:01,070
It's a bit worrying
that you don't seem that driven.

105
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,400
Not interested?
That's not true at all.

106
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:08,170
If possible,
I'd really like the position.

107
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:10,740
Is there any way
you can make it happen?

108
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,240
Well...

109
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:16,310
For that to happen,
I'd have to pull a lot of strings.

110
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,920
If you can just get me
appointed as director,

111
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:21,690
I won't forget this favor, Ms. Joo.

112
00:06:23,690 --> 00:06:24,890
I'll think about it.

113
00:06:30,930 --> 00:06:33,360
(Purchasing Department)

114
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,520
The Purchasing Department
locks its door during lunch.

115
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:56,620
They're sensitive
about the expenditure records.

116
00:06:57,020 --> 00:06:58,790
Right, I see.

117
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,760
And you are...

118
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,160
Right.

119
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:04,260
Hello.

120
00:07:04,330 --> 00:07:06,560
I'm Ko Eun Seol,
a new hire in the Design Team.

121
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,330
You must be the winner
of the recent competition.

122
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:11,700
Nice to meet you.

123
00:07:11,770 --> 00:07:13,810
I'm Na Tae Hoon,
Public Relations Manager.

124
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,510
Right, it's nice to meet you.

125
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:21,650
So what brings a new hire
from the Design Team here?

126
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,620
I'm friends with Manager Choi
in the Purchasing Department.

127
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:27,720
Want me to give him a message?

128
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,020
That's all right.

129
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:35,060
I was just passing by and figured
I'd say hi if anyone was here.

130
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:37,730
Well, I'll see you around.

131
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:52,010
I bet you were surprised
to get my call.

132
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:55,280
Is there something
you wanted to discuss?

133
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:02,220
I heard you told the CEO
you intend to marry our Hae Ra.

134
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:05,020
Yes.

135
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:07,430
I admire your drive,

136
00:08:07,690 --> 00:08:09,730
but don't you think your technique
is a bit lacking?

137
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,560
Excuse me?

138
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:15,170
I heard you couldn't answer
when he asked if you love her.

139
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:17,130
When I heard that,

140
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,570
I'll admit
I was a little disappointed too.

141
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:22,910
I'm sorry.

142
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,680
Hae Ra...

143
00:08:27,250 --> 00:08:28,750
Do you really not love her?

144
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,520
To be honest...

145
00:08:34,490 --> 00:08:35,590
I'm not sure.

146
00:08:37,990 --> 00:08:39,260
Even so,

147
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:42,290
you aren't trying to marry Hae Ra
just for her background,

148
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:43,490
right?

149
00:08:44,430 --> 00:08:45,500
That's not it at all.

150
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,430
I'm fond of Hae Ra,

151
00:08:47,770 --> 00:08:49,930
and I'm confident
I can be a faithful husband.

152
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Good.

153
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:54,970
You know, Chief Cha,

154
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:57,110
I like how you're
so honest and sincere.

155
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,280
But my husband is a different story.

156
00:09:00,510 --> 00:09:02,910
He'd prefer you tell
a little white lie.

157
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:06,480
I understand what you're saying.

158
00:09:08,690 --> 00:09:10,350
I trust you, Chief Cha.

159
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:12,160
And I also think...

160
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:14,530
there's no one better
for Hae Ra than you.

161
00:09:16,690 --> 00:09:17,730
But,

162
00:09:18,030 --> 00:09:20,970
you know we can't proceed
without my husband's approval, right?

163
00:09:22,430 --> 00:09:23,430
Of course.

164
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:25,000
So,

165
00:09:25,470 --> 00:09:28,370
make an effort
to change the CEO's mind.

166
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:31,580
Come over to the house
on the weekends.

167
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:34,710
Understood, ma'am.

168
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,280
Good.

169
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:46,320
Assistant Manager Lee.

170
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:48,890
This is
a fabric sample request form.

171
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:50,390
Take this to the Purchasing Manager.

172
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:51,430
Sure, Ms. Kang.

173
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:56,130
Yes, hello?

174
00:09:57,370 --> 00:09:58,370
Yes.

175
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:05,340
- Mr. Lee.
- Hey, Eun Seol.

176
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:08,110
Do you mind
if I deliver those documents?

177
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:09,650
You?

178
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:11,620
Yes. I haven't had a chance
to introduce myself...

179
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,020
to the Purchasing Manager yet.

180
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:14,820
All right, then.

181
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:17,990
Wait.

182
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:22,630
I'd prefer if you didn't
mention this to Ms. Kang.

183
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:25,230
Got it.

184
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,900
Manager Na. Hello.

185
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:41,850
Yes, come in.

186
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:48,220
Hello.

187
00:10:48,490 --> 00:10:50,790
I'm Ko Eun Seol,
the Design Team's new hire.

188
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:54,430
Are you the new hire
from the special recruitment?

189
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:55,730
Yes.

190
00:10:55,930 --> 00:10:59,060
Here. The Team Leader
asked me to deliver this.

191
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:00,530
Right, the sample request.

192
00:11:02,170 --> 00:11:04,370
Also, would you like some coffee?

193
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:06,370
Coffee sounds great.

194
00:11:06,370 --> 00:11:08,410
I was just thinking
I could use a cup.

195
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:11,080
Perfect. Thank you, I'll enjoy it.

196
00:11:14,910 --> 00:11:17,050
Oh no.

197
00:11:17,650 --> 00:11:20,080
I'm so sorry, sir.
Are you all right?

198
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,250
I'm fine.

199
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:23,690
You should rinse it
with water right away.

200
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,360
I should.

201
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,260
Just leave the documents here.

202
00:11:29,490 --> 00:11:31,300
I'm so sorry, sir.

203
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:33,030
This was expensive, darn it.

204
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:49,850
(June 5: Day off)

205
00:11:55,350 --> 00:11:57,490
Did you have a lot of fun
at taekwondo today?

206
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:00,760
- Yes, it was a lot of fun.
- Really?

207
00:12:01,290 --> 00:12:02,360
Mister!

208
00:12:06,830 --> 00:12:09,000
- Are you coming from taekwondo?
- Yes.

209
00:12:10,770 --> 00:12:12,370
You know, I'm good at taekwondo too.

210
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:14,140
Want me to teach you?

211
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:16,140
Really? I'd love that.

212
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:17,610
Why would you agree to that?

213
00:12:18,010 --> 00:12:21,050
Look, can't you work out
at the gym instead?

214
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:23,380
Why?

215
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:26,120
Isn't it way too hot
to exercise out here?

216
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:27,790
That's the best part.

217
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:30,550
When you get a good sweat like this
and then shower, it's so refreshing.

218
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:34,630
Mister, your muscles are awesome.

219
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,830
Really? Want to feel them?

220
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:39,100
Yes.

221
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:41,900
Hey, Teun Teun.

222
00:12:42,430 --> 00:12:44,000
You shouldn't touch things
like that.

223
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:51,010
- Things like that?
- Why can't I touch them, Mom?

224
00:12:51,210 --> 00:12:52,340
Anyway,

225
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:55,010
that kind of thing isn't cool,
it's gross.

226
00:12:55,010 --> 00:12:56,210
Let's just go inside.

227
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:01,250
So prickly.

228
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,270
You worked out looking like that?

229
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:16,770
Yes. Why?

230
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:19,840
What if Teun Teun's mom saw you?

231
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:21,610
She was already complaining.

232
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:24,340
Do I really look that weird?

233
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,740
It's not that it's weird.

234
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:27,780
I'm worried she might start
drooling over you.

235
00:13:28,310 --> 00:13:31,080
Don't go stirring up feelings
in that woman for no reason.

236
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:33,080
Grandma, please.

237
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,950
Oh, for goodness' sake.

238
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:39,620
Mom, you worry
about the strangest things.

239
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:42,360
That's because you don't get it.

240
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:46,930
Man or a woman, do you think
anyone's immune to a handsome face?

241
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:50,600
Then, should I be careful too?

242
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:53,940
Who'd ever hit on you?

243
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:04,050
Hey, are you just getting home?

244
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:07,380
- Yes.
- Why do you seem so down?

245
00:14:08,090 --> 00:14:09,390
Whatever.

246
00:14:11,090 --> 00:14:12,860
I'm sure you heard from Seok Jin.

247
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:14,930
About what?

248
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:18,260
Didn't he tell you he's coming over
to our house this weekend?

249
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,630
He's coming over?

250
00:14:21,270 --> 00:14:22,400
You didn't know?

251
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,070
Is something going on
between you two?

252
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:26,470
I assumed he'd tell you.

253
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:30,170
What could be going on?
Anyway, I got it.

254
00:14:43,850 --> 00:14:45,790
So I guess he feels bad after all.

255
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,900
Seok Jin's coming over this weekend.

256
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,870
You don't have any plans, do you?

257
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:01,940
I told you to look into
blind dates for Hae Ra,

258
00:15:02,010 --> 00:15:03,770
and you invited
Seok Jin over instead?

259
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,510
What do you mean, invited?

260
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,510
He wanted to come over,

261
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:08,850
so how could I say no?

262
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:11,080
Tell him not to come.

263
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,350
Honey.

264
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:16,690
Let's just have a relaxing weekend.

265
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:20,560
Why wouldn't you be able to relax
just because Seok Jin's here?

266
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:24,090
You two can grab a drink
and kick back.

267
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:28,170
You've been acting weird lately.

268
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:29,970
How so?

269
00:15:30,270 --> 00:15:32,000
You used to listen to me
unconditionally.

270
00:15:32,170 --> 00:15:33,470
What's gotten into you lately?

271
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:36,610
I'm glad you brought that up.

272
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:40,240
Since I've always done
whatever you say,

273
00:15:40,310 --> 00:15:43,110
it's time you listened to me.
Understand?

274
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:45,550
What's gotten into you?

275
00:15:46,650 --> 00:15:49,150
In any case, don't make plans
for the weekend.

276
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,400
He took the day off?

277
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,200
Yes.

278
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:04,030
That means
the Purchasing Manager has no alibi.

279
00:16:04,030 --> 00:16:05,400
How do we figure out where he was?

280
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:09,010
We'll have to confront him directly.

281
00:16:09,870 --> 00:16:10,870
How?

282
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,080
That's for us to figure out.

283
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:18,480
Figure out what?

284
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,650
- Dad!
- Mr. Ko.

285
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:25,090
What do you need to figure out?

286
00:16:27,390 --> 00:16:29,230
Dad, it's nothing.

287
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:33,330
Tell me.
What have you two been up to lately?

288
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,470
What do you mean?

289
00:16:36,730 --> 00:16:38,270
I said it's nothing.

290
00:16:38,470 --> 00:16:40,200
Do you think I'm an idiot?

291
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:41,910
You've been at this for days,

292
00:16:42,170 --> 00:16:44,780
meeting up like a pair of spies.

293
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:47,540
What... It's nothing serious, sir.

294
00:16:47,610 --> 00:16:50,450
Are you going to treat me
like an idiot too, Attorney Seo?

295
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:53,350
No, it's not that.

296
00:16:56,190 --> 00:17:00,420
Eun Seol.
I think we should tell your father.

297
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:04,500
The thing is, sir...

298
00:17:07,870 --> 00:17:08,870
What?

299
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:11,470
Wait, so...

300
00:17:11,970 --> 00:17:15,340
You joined Cheongma not for the job,

301
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,880
but to catch the real killer?

302
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:21,180
Yes.

303
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:27,080
If that's the case...

304
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:28,220
Quit right now.

305
00:17:29,450 --> 00:17:30,550
Dad.

306
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,020
This is the person
who killed your mom.

307
00:17:33,490 --> 00:17:35,630
They're a very dangerous person.

308
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:37,430
And you're going to take them on?

309
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:39,800
No, it's too dangerous.
Absolutely not!

310
00:17:40,430 --> 00:17:42,430
I'll be fine, Dad.

311
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,170
What do you mean you'll be fine?

312
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:48,840
What if something terrible happens
to you too?

313
00:17:48,910 --> 00:17:51,880
But Eun Seol has
to clear her name, sir.

314
00:17:55,310 --> 00:17:56,610
Clear her name?

315
00:17:57,380 --> 00:18:00,220
She can't live the rest of her life
being framed as a murderer.

316
00:18:02,590 --> 00:18:05,320
Well, that's true, but...

317
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:08,590
That's right, Dad.

318
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:12,300
I have to catch the real killer
and get justice for Mom.

319
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:15,570
But more than anything,
I want to know the truth.

320
00:18:17,370 --> 00:18:20,070
So please,
just look the other way, Dad.

321
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:27,950
Then...

322
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,550
I'll help you.

323
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:32,720
You will?

324
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:36,020
Don't, Dad.
You don't have to get involved.

325
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:38,790
I can't let you face
this danger alone.

326
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:42,060
Tell me. What can I do?

327
00:18:49,530 --> 00:18:50,830
- Dad.
- Yes.

328
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:52,340
Are you sure you can do this?

329
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:55,870
Leave it to me. I have a plan.

330
00:19:07,250 --> 00:19:08,250
Hello.

331
00:19:09,090 --> 00:19:12,060
I'll return your necklace,
so let's meet now.

332
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,040
Here.

333
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:31,680
Thank you.

334
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:39,050
So...

335
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:41,950
Are you still not going to tell me?

336
00:19:44,050 --> 00:19:45,060
Can you just...

337
00:19:46,090 --> 00:19:48,160
look the other way?

338
00:19:51,430 --> 00:19:52,730
Is that what you want me to do?

339
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:57,800
Yes.

340
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:01,710
All right.

341
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:03,910
If that's what you want, I will.

342
00:20:05,310 --> 00:20:06,310
I'm sorry.

343
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,720
I trust you.

344
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:15,520
But,

345
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:17,920
this time, when you're ready,

346
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:20,760
please tell me in good time.

347
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:26,960
Thank you.

348
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:41,450
I trust you.

349
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:44,380
But,

350
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:46,720
this time, when you're ready,

351
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,620
please tell me in good time.

352
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:12,580
Aren't you getting lunch?

353
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:14,280
I'm going to.

354
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:17,380
I heard you're coming
to my house this weekend.

355
00:21:17,750 --> 00:21:18,750
Yes.

356
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:22,620
Is that your way
of apologizing to me?

357
00:21:26,190 --> 00:21:28,060
I have nothing
to apologize to you for.

358
00:21:29,090 --> 00:21:30,560
- Seok Jin.
- Kang Hae Ra.

359
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,600
Don't you trust me?

360
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,030
Have I failed to earn your trust?

361
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:37,970
That's not it.

362
00:21:37,970 --> 00:21:40,940
If that's not it,
then don't be like this again.

363
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:43,640
I really hate it
when you act like this.

364
00:21:43,710 --> 00:21:45,810
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

365
00:21:45,810 --> 00:21:46,810
Got it?

366
00:21:48,050 --> 00:21:50,510
Whatever. I'm hungry,
so hurry up and come out.

367
00:21:50,650 --> 00:21:53,180
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

368
00:22:06,230 --> 00:22:07,300
Excuse me.

369
00:22:08,430 --> 00:22:09,630
What's this about?

370
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:11,840
Oh, right.

371
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,470
I'm with the police.

372
00:22:16,670 --> 00:22:19,880
You're Manager Choi Jun Hyeok
at Cheongma, right?

373
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:23,010
Yes, I'm Choi Jun Hyeok, but...

374
00:22:24,380 --> 00:22:26,020
What do the police want with me?

375
00:22:32,890 --> 00:22:34,420
You recognize this car, don't you?

376
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:37,230
That looks like
one of our company cars.

377
00:22:38,430 --> 00:22:40,100
Is there a problem with it?

378
00:22:42,100 --> 00:22:46,240
On June 5, this car was involved
in an accident...

379
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:48,640
and was reported as a hit-and-run.

380
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:52,140
We're looking for the person
who was driving the car at the time.

381
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,340
A hit-and-run?

382
00:22:55,050 --> 00:22:57,350
I didn't do anything like that.

383
00:23:00,250 --> 00:23:02,020
What were you doing on June 5?

384
00:23:03,250 --> 00:23:05,460
How am I supposed to remember
what I did three months ago?

385
00:23:06,820 --> 00:23:07,820
Just try.

386
00:23:10,190 --> 00:23:11,500
Wait a second.

387
00:23:16,670 --> 00:23:19,200
I took the day off that day.

388
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:23,240
We already knew that.

389
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:25,340
You knew?

390
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:26,840
How?

391
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:29,180
I'm the one asking questions here.

392
00:23:29,350 --> 00:23:32,080
Now, remember what you did
on your day off.

393
00:23:33,550 --> 00:23:35,950
I usually go hiking on my days off.

394
00:23:36,650 --> 00:23:37,650
On that day off,

395
00:23:37,650 --> 00:23:40,090
I went hiking on Mount Seorak
with my friends.

396
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:44,090
Hiking? On Mount Seorak?

397
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:45,260
Wait a minute.

398
00:23:46,100 --> 00:23:49,100
Can I see your police ID again?

399
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:52,570
My ID? Why?

400
00:23:54,100 --> 00:23:55,210
You...

401
00:23:56,070 --> 00:23:57,410
Are you really the police?

402
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,210
Of course I am.

403
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,910
I'm the one who asks the questions.

404
00:24:04,450 --> 00:24:05,680
Unbelievable.

405
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:07,780
Well, I think I'll be going now.

406
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:09,920
Look here. Hey!

407
00:24:12,290 --> 00:24:14,320
Look at what? Don't "hey" me.

408
00:24:15,990 --> 00:24:17,930
Here. You see this?

409
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:20,100
You see this?

410
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:23,300
She's been looking into
the department managers?

411
00:24:24,270 --> 00:24:25,270
How cute.

412
00:24:25,670 --> 00:24:28,340
She'll soon be coming
to check my schedule.

413
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:32,580
I'll make sure Ko Eun Seol
has nothing to find.

414
00:24:33,810 --> 00:24:34,850
That you should.

415
00:24:37,950 --> 00:24:40,280
Ms. Joo, is something on your mind?

416
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:42,990
It's just that...

417
00:24:43,350 --> 00:24:46,020
I want to see it for myself
at least once.

418
00:24:47,390 --> 00:24:49,530
I want to see her believe
that crawling into Cheongma...

419
00:24:50,390 --> 00:24:51,860
and working hard...

420
00:24:51,930 --> 00:24:54,970
is all it takes to find
what she's looking for.

421
00:24:57,830 --> 00:25:01,170
Seriously.
Earlier, my heart was really...

422
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:03,440
I thought it was going to jump
right out of my chest.

423
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,110
You did a great job, Dad.

424
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:08,450
I really pulled it off, didn't I?

425
00:25:09,050 --> 00:25:12,120
Of course. You did a fantastic job.

426
00:25:13,780 --> 00:25:15,850
So, what should I do next?

427
00:25:16,520 --> 00:25:18,960
Dad, you don't have to do
anything else.

428
00:25:19,060 --> 00:25:22,890
Why? I'm a natural.
Just tell me what to do.

429
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:24,930
I'll carry it out perfectly.

430
00:25:25,100 --> 00:25:26,900
What are you going
to carry out perfectly?

431
00:25:26,930 --> 00:25:28,300
Mom, you...

432
00:25:28,330 --> 00:25:30,570
- Did you hear me?
- Unbelievable.

433
00:25:31,100 --> 00:25:35,310
Goodness, what are you all plotting,
whispering together every night?

434
00:25:36,070 --> 00:25:37,940
Hey, that watermelon
looks delicious.

435
00:25:38,510 --> 00:25:39,640
It looks good.

436
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:42,650
- Mom, it's nothing.
- Yes?

437
00:25:42,650 --> 00:25:44,580
Let's take this inside and enjoy it.

438
00:25:44,580 --> 00:25:47,580
We'll go in first.
You should finish your chat.

439
00:25:47,780 --> 00:25:49,320
- Come on.
- No, I don't want to.

440
00:25:49,390 --> 00:25:51,720
- We'll enjoy ours alone.
- Why?

441
00:26:00,630 --> 00:26:01,870
We're almost at the finish line.

442
00:26:03,700 --> 00:26:04,800
It seems so.

443
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:14,210
Director Han submitted
his resignation today.

444
00:26:14,910 --> 00:26:16,580
He told me, actually.

445
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:19,120
He's wrapping everything up
and moving out of the city.

446
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:22,090
Who should we get to replace him?

447
00:26:22,250 --> 00:26:24,490
Don't worry.
I've already spoken to someone.

448
00:26:25,090 --> 00:26:27,320
- You did?
- Yes. Why?

449
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:30,730
Well, I was planning
on finding someone this time.

450
00:26:31,030 --> 00:26:34,460
What does it matter who finds them?
As long as they're qualified, right?

451
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:37,070
You know my friend,
Bae Jong Min, right?

452
00:26:37,430 --> 00:26:39,270
The writer
and current affairs commentator.

453
00:26:40,740 --> 00:26:42,010
You want to appoint Jong Min?

454
00:26:42,670 --> 00:26:44,210
As far as I know,

455
00:26:44,210 --> 00:26:47,410
he's an active advisor
at a broadcasting station.

456
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:50,380
Won't there be
a conflict of interest?

457
00:26:50,380 --> 00:26:51,480
Just in case,

458
00:26:51,550 --> 00:26:53,280
I told him to quit
his advisor position.

459
00:26:54,550 --> 00:26:57,820
So let's just go
with my friend this time. All right?

460
00:26:57,850 --> 00:27:00,090
Sure. If you say so.

461
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:09,470
Ms. Kang,
I'll stop by the factory tomorrow...

462
00:27:09,530 --> 00:27:10,530
before coming in.

463
00:27:11,170 --> 00:27:12,170
Whatever.

464
00:27:12,670 --> 00:27:15,070
We'll be heading out now, then.

465
00:27:15,940 --> 00:27:17,210
Okay, see you tomorrow.

466
00:27:21,950 --> 00:27:23,180
Aren't you leaving?

467
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:26,450
I still have some work to do.

468
00:27:27,420 --> 00:27:28,750
You can go ahead and leave,
Ms. Kang.

469
00:27:30,220 --> 00:27:31,320
What's your deal?

470
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:33,420
What do you mean?

471
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:36,860
You work late every day.
Do you have some other motive?

472
00:27:38,030 --> 00:27:39,330
Another motive?

473
00:27:40,930 --> 00:27:42,030
I don't have one.

474
00:27:42,700 --> 00:27:44,870
Just leave already.
I can't stand the sight of you.

475
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:48,710
Sure.

476
00:27:49,310 --> 00:27:50,710
Then I'll be leaving now.

477
00:27:57,110 --> 00:28:00,450
Who does she think she is?
She's so annoying.

478
00:28:31,110 --> 00:28:32,950
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

479
00:28:58,840 --> 00:28:59,840
(Na Tae Hoon)

480
00:29:20,460 --> 00:29:21,700
(6099)

481
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:23,700
(Na Tae Hoon, Welcome)

482
00:29:33,580 --> 00:29:35,880
(Cheongma General Affairs Data,
Cheongma Vehicle Management)

483
00:29:41,820 --> 00:29:42,820
(Cheongma PR Department:
Document Index)

484
00:29:42,890 --> 00:29:44,450
(Weekly PR Report)

485
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:09,480
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

486
00:30:37,170 --> 00:30:38,170
Ms. Joo.

487
00:31:12,910 --> 00:31:16,810
(A Trap Called Desire)

488
00:31:16,810 --> 00:31:18,980
I doubt you came here
just to chat with me.

489
00:31:19,050 --> 00:31:20,380
So why are you here today?

490
00:31:20,520 --> 00:31:22,620
Didn't you tell him
you wanted to marry me?

491
00:31:22,690 --> 00:31:23,690
Didn't you?

492
00:31:23,750 --> 00:31:26,890
Dating? That's when you become
boyfriend and girlfriend.

493
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:29,560
That shameless woman is making
a move on him, isn't she?

494
00:31:29,630 --> 00:31:31,730
I need to give her a warning.
This won't do.

495
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:32,930
The last person is the one...

496
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,900
we couldn't confirm
because of Director Joo.

497
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:37,530
So tomorrow, we'll find out
who the real killer is?

498
00:31:37,700 --> 00:31:41,000
Director Joo is someone
I couldn't do without.

499
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:42,640
It's amusing.

500
00:31:42,710 --> 00:31:44,910
She thinks she's being clever,
but she'll tire herself out.

501
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:48,080
He must be desperate, seeing
as he's throwing money around.

502
00:31:48,710 --> 00:31:50,710
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
